Alternative: distinguish by total measure? The measures live on different types, not an invariant of the metric space alone. Distinguish by `Metric.diam`: an isometry equivalence preserves diam (`IsometryEquiv.diam_image`?). diam (AddCircle 1) = 1/2 vs diam (AddCircle 2) = 1. Proving these diam values requires the bound ≤ T/2 (again).

Proving `diam (AddCircle T) ≤ T/2` (for T > 0): use the representatives trick: for x y, `dist x y = ‖x - y‖` and for z = x - y, choose representative r ∈ [0,T) of z, then `‖z‖ ≤ min(r, T-r) ≤ T/2`. Need: `‖z‖ ≤ T - r` — via `z = ↑r`, so `z = ↑(r - T)` as well? `(r - T : AddCircle T) = (r : AddCircle T)` since T ≡ 0. Then `‖z‖ ≤ |r - T| = T - r` (as r ≤ T). And `‖z‖ ≤ r` via norm_mk_le_norm + |r| = r. Then `‖z‖ ≤ min r (T - r) ≤ T/2`. This requires `r ≤ T` (from Ico: r < 0 + T ✓) and `r ≥ 0` ✓, then `min r (T-r) ≤ T/2` by linarith.

