Actually, better than a schema: I can prove a *single theorem* over a family `t : Set GHSpace` of the form `t = {p | ∃ T ∈ Icc 1 2, p = toGHSpace (AddCircle T)}` — but the measure assignment problem (choosing T per p) returns. The schema approach avoids that.

